# Economic Prediction Framework — FRED-Enhanced Audit

**Branch:** manager-audit/cde006-canonical-kc-20260523  
**Last updated:** 2026-05-24  
**Data:** 29 FRED series + 10 Yahoo Finance tickers, 2014–2026, 149 months  
**Validation:** Walk-forward only (no look-ahead). Diebold-Mariano (regression) / McNemar (classification) significance tests. Regime-stratified: Pre-COVID (<2020-03), COVID (2020-03–2022-01), Post-COVID (≥2022-01).

---

## Core Finding

**None of the 5 phases produce a robust, statistically significant edge across all market regimes.** The only significant result is Phase 1 CPI in the Pre-COVID regime (DM p=0.023). All other results are either non-significant or actively harmful.

This is the honest answer to "can we predict economic releases before they happen?" — **sometimes, in stable regimes, with the right leading indicators. Never robustly across regime shifts.**

---

## Phase 1 — CPI Prediction

**Target:** Next month's CPI MoM %  
**Best model:** Random Forest with FRED features  
**Dataset:** 144 months (2014–2026), walk-forward test n=108

### Key Features (by correlation with target)
| Feature | r | Interpretation |
|---------|---|----------------|
| CPIAUCSL_MOM (lag) | +0.550 | CPI momentum — strongest single predictor |
| PCEPI_MOM | +0.548 | PCE leads CPI by ~1 month |
| PPIACO_MOM | +0.544 | Commodity input costs pass through |
| YF_DBC_RET | +0.538 | Commodity ETF — market-priced input costs |
| CPILFESL_MOM | +0.493 | Core CPI momentum |
| T10YIEM | +0.461 | 10yr breakeven = market's CPI forecast |
| MICH | +0.395 | Michigan inflation expectations |

### Walk-Forward Results
| Era | n | Naive RMSE | RF RMSE | DM p | Verdict |
|-----|---|-----------|---------|------|---------|
| All | 108 | 0.2762% | 0.2453% | 0.197 | Marginal, unproven |
| Pre-COVID | 35 | 0.2038% | 0.1503% | **0.023 ✓** | **Significant** |
| COVID | 22 | 0.2765% | 0.2903% | 0.809 | RF worse (noise regime) |
| Post-COVID | 51 | 0.3163% | 0.2750% | 0.267 | Beats naive, not significant |

### Interpretation
- Pre-COVID: PPI/PCE/commodity signals have genuine predictive power in stable inflation regimes
- COVID: All models fail — supply chain shocks break the input-cost → CPI relationship
- Post-COVID: RF beats naive but not significantly (n=51, high variance from rate-hike era)
- **Do not use this model during regime transitions**

