## Phase 2 — NFP Prediction

**Target:** Next month's Nonfarm Payrolls MoM (thousands)  
**Best model:** RF with IC4WSA (4-week avg initial claims)  
**Dataset:** Post-COVID regime-aware (train 2022+)

### Results
| Era | n | Naive RMSE | RF RMSE | DM p | Verdict |
|-----|---|-----------|---------|------|---------|
| Post-COVID | 33 | 110k | 120k | 0.382 | RF worse |

### Key Finding
- IC4WSA r=-0.957 with NFP (COVID contaminated by CARES Act claims spike)
- Without COVID: r=-0.490 (genuine signal)
- Post-COVID regime-aware RF corr=0.573 (direction right) but RMSE worse than naive
- **Root cause:** NFP has ~100k noise floor from birth-death model. Without ADP (2-day lead) and ISM PMI, the model can't beat naive on magnitude.
- **Verdict: No edge. Model incomplete without ADP/ISM.**

---

## Phase 3 — Yield Direction

**Target:** 10yr Treasury yield direction next month (up/down)  
**Best model:** Logistic Regression with FRED yield features  
**Dataset:** 146 months (2014–2026), walk-forward test n=110

### Walk-Forward Results
| Era | n | Majority class | Logit | McNemar p | Verdict |
|-----|---|---------------|-------|-----------|---------|
| All | 110 | 53.6% | 54.5% | 1.000 | No edge |
| Pre-COVID | 37 | 51.4% | 70.3% | 0.096 | Marginal |
| COVID | 22 | 59.1% | 54.5% | 1.000 | No edge |
| Post-COVID | 51 | 52.9% | 43.1% | 0.472 | **Model inverts** |

### Critical Finding: Post-COVID Regime Inversion
The model trained on "higher inflation → higher yields" breaks post-2022. After the Fed pivot, the model predicts DOWN when yields are actually going UP (27 actual UP, logit calls only 20 UP out of 51). **Using this model post-2022 would actively lose money.**

### Top Predictors
HYG return (credit stress), DGS10 level, Core CPI MoM, DBC return, SPY return

**Verdict: No robust edge. Pre-COVID signal doesn't survive regime shifts.**

