## Phase 4 — Equity Regime Prediction

**Target:** SPY regime next month (UPTREND/DOWNTREND/CHOPPY)  
**Best model:** RF with balanced class weights, VIX + Sahm proxy + yield slope  
**Dataset:** 130 months (2014–2025), walk-forward test n=94

### Walk-Forward Results
| Era | n | Majority class | RF (balanced) | McNemar p | Verdict |
|-----|---|---------------|---------------|-----------|---------|
| All | 94 | 60.6% | 45.7% | **0.006** | **RF significantly WORSE** |
| Pre-COVID | 27 | 55.6% | 44.4% | 0.450 | No edge |
| COVID | 22 | 68.2% | 54.5% | 0.371 | No edge |
| Post-COVID | 45 | 60.0% | 42.2% | **0.027** | **RF significantly WORSE** |

### McNemar Direction Check
- b (RF gains over naive): 4
- c (RF loses vs naive): 18
- **Net: RF loses 14 more cases than naive**

### Classification Report (All periods)
| Class | Precision | Recall | F1 |
|-------|-----------|--------|-----|
| CHOPPY | 0.38 | 0.27 | 0.32 |
| DOWNTREND | 0.07 | 0.04 | 0.05 |
| UPTREND | 0.55 | 0.68 | 0.61 |

DOWNTREND recall=4% — the model essentially cannot identify downtrends.

### Root Cause
Balanced class_weight forces the model to predict minority classes (DOWNTREND, CHOPPY) more often, which actively hurts accuracy in an UPTREND-dominated dataset (57.7% UPTREND). The macro features don't have enough signal to overcome the base rate.

**Verdict: No edge. Model is actively harmful vs majority-class baseline.**

### Connection to `_compute_regime()` in main.py
Phase 4 uses monthly macro data to predict next-month SPY regime. `_compute_regime()` uses same-day intraday data to label current regime. These are different time horizons and different feature sets — **do not conflate them.** Monthly macro prediction cannot replace intraday regime detection.

