## Phase 5 — GDP Nowcast

**Target:** Real GDP QoQ growth % (quarterly)  
**Best model:** RF with monthly leading indicators (last month of quarter)  
**Dataset:** 44 quarters (2014–2025), walk-forward test n=32

### Walk-Forward Results
| Era | n | Naive RMSE | RF RMSE | DM p | Verdict |
|-----|---|-----------|---------|------|---------|
| All | 32 | 2.089% | 2.213% | 0.244 | RF worse |
| Pre-COVID | 10 | 0.691% | 0.625% | 0.292 | Beats naive (n too small) |
| COVID | 7 | 4.347% | 4.621% | 0.261 | RF worse |
| Post-COVID | 15 | 0.421% | 0.472% | 0.374 | RF worse |

### Top Predictors
CLAIMS_TREND (0.225), SAHM_PROXY (0.209), PAYEMS_MOM (0.143), UNRATE (0.140), HOUST_MOM (0.104)

### Key Finding
- COVID quarters (Q2 2020: -7.9%, Q3 2020: +7.8%) dominate RMSE and make all-period comparison nearly meaningless
- Pre-COVID RF corr=0.628 is genuinely interesting but n=10 is too small for significance
- Naive baseline = historical mean GDP growth (appropriate for mean-reverting quarterly series)
- **Verdict: No edge. COVID outliers overwhelm the signal. Need ISM PMI and ADP for real nowcasting.**

